  "question": {
    "text": "The total number of unpaired electrons present in the complex <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>Cr</mi><mo>(</mo><mtext>oxalate</mtext><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> is______."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Cr</mi><mo>(</mo><mtext>&#160;oxalate&#160;</mtext><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math><br />Chromium is in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math> oxidation state.</p><p>It has stable&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow/></msubsup><mo>&#160;</mo></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;configuration</p><p>Number of unpaired electrons in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cr</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math> will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p>"
